          %p
            For more see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+finiteness+theorem"} Serre finiteness theorem
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} homotopy groups of spheres
          %h3#bundles_over_the_4sphere Bundles over the 4-sphere
          %h4#the_quaternionic_hopf_fibration The quaternionic Hopf fibration
          %p
            The 4-sphere participates in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+fibration"} Hopf fibration
            with the field of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            replaced by the division ring of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            or Hamiltonian numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℍ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 7
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 4
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi SU
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S^3 &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; S^7
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^\mathrlap{p}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; S^4 &amp;\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathbf{B} SU(2)
                  }
          %p
            Here the idea is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
            may be construed as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 7
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℍ
                            %mn 4
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ∈
                          %msup
                            %mi ℍ
                            %mn 2
                          %mo :
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 2
                          %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mn 2
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S^7
                  \&amp;\simeq
                  S(\mathbb{H}^4)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq
                  \\{(x, y) \in \mathbb{H}^2: {|x|}^2 + {|y|}^2 = 1\},
                  }
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            mapping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x/y
            as an element in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+line"} projective line
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℙ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{H}) \cong S^4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsor"} torsor
            parameterized by quaternionic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalars"} scalars
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            of unit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
            (so
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in S^3
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
            = succeed "-bundle)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4 \to \mathbf{B} SU(2)
          %p#HopfParameterization
            There are other useful ways to parameterize the quaternionic Hopf fibration, such as the original
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+construction"} Hopf construction
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Hopf+construction#HopfFibrations"} Hopf fibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            is identified as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4 \simeq S(\mathbb{R} \oplus \mathbb{H})
          %h4#the_calabipenrose_fibration The Calabi-Penrose fibration
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Penrose+fibration"} Calabi-Penrose fibration
          %h4#AsAQuotientOfTheComplexProjectivePlane The complex projective plane
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnold-Kuiper-Massey+theorem"}> Arnold-Kuiper-Massey theorem
                )
            %p
              The 4-sphere is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+plane"} complex projective plane
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+conjugation"} complex conjugation
              (on homogeneous coordinates):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{C}P^2 / (-)^*
                    \\simeq
                    S^4
          %h3#exotic_smooth_structures Exotic smooth structures
          %p
            It is open whether the 4-sphere admits an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+smooth+structure"} exotic smooth structure
            %a{:href => "#FreedmanGompfMorrisonWalker09"} Freedman, Gompf, Morrison &amp; Walker 2009
            for review.
          %h3#QuaternionAction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
            action
          %p
            If we identify
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 5
                  %msub
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℚ
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi ℍ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^5 \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{R} \oplus \mathbb{H}
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real vector space
            underlying the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^4 \simeq S(\mathbb{R} \oplus \mathbb{H})
          %p
            as in the discussion of the quaternionic Hopf fibration
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HopfParameterization"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} SU(2)
            on the 4-sphere, by identifying
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SU(2) \simeq S(\mathbb{Q})
          %p and then acting by left multiplication.
          %h4#CircleAction Circle action
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Given an continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-sphere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
              space is of one of two types:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  either it is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ↪
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0 \hookrightarrow S^4
              %li
                %p
                  or it has the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy type
                  of an even-dimensional sphere.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#FelixOpreaTanre08"}> Félix-Oprea-Tanré 08, Example 7.39
            )
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+actions+on+spheres"} group actions on spheres
          %p
            As a special case of the
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#QuaternionAction"} above
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^1 \simeq U(1) \hookrightarrow SU(2)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Consider the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+action+on+an+n-sphere"} group action on the 4-sphere
          #CircleActionOn4Sphere.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                \-action on 4-sphere)
            %p Regard
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^4 \simeq S(\mathbb{R} \oplus \mathbb{H})
            %p
              as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+sphere"} unit sphere
              inside the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              (as
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+spaces"} real vector spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              with the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+group"} special unitary group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
              as the group of unit-norm quaternions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SU(2) \simeq S(\mathbb{H},\cdot)
            %p
              In particular this restricts to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^1 \simeq U(1) \hookrightarrow SU(2)
            %p
              (as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+matrices"} diagonal matrices
              inside
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
          %p
            The resulting ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ord
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4/_{ord} S^1 \simeq S^3
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4 \to S^3
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension"} suspension
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Hopf+fibration"} complex Hopf fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \to S^2
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            set of the action is the two poles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ±
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi ℍ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^0 \;=\; \{(\pm 1, 0,0,0,0)\} \;\in\; \mathbb{R} \oplus \mathbb{H}
          %p
            introduced by the suspension, hence forms the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
            space. Since this is not the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+set"} empty set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4 // S^1
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+action"} circle action
            differs from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^4//S^1 \longrightarrow S^4 / S^1 \simeq S^3
                  \\,.
          %p
            Hence both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4 // S^1
            are canonically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+dg-module"} minimal dg-module
            presentation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            for these projections is given in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#RoigSaralegiAranguren00"} Roig &amp; Saralegi-Aranguren 00, second page
          #FourSphereOverThreeSphereMinimalDgModel.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#RoigSaralegiAranguren00"}> Roig &amp; Saralegi-Aranguren 00, p. 2
                )
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Sym
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
